{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,14.011,1.643,1.471,"US Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"21 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,31.229,3.651,3.268,"Viking Therapeutics"],[13.889,14.731,37.088,2.373,2.124,"Priced for failure ahead of Phase 3 data"],[13.889,20.845,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Viking closed at $24.77, 41% below its July high, 29% below the $35.00 at"],[13.889,22.289,52.934,1.809,1.634,"which it sold 9.0m shares in September and under the lowest of 19 Street targets"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"($34; mean $95). Enterprise value is $2.46bn, 35% of the $7.0bn Pfizer paid up"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"front for Metsera a year ago. In our model the price needs only a 24% chance"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"that injectable VK2735 is approved; the base rate for a metabolic drug in Phase"],[13.889,28.065,52.936,1.809,1.634,"3 is 56% and we use 65%. We rate VKTX Overweight, Dec-27 target $71. That"],[13.889,29.509,52.931,1.809,1.634,"is an expected value: Phase 3 data are due in 2027, after which we would value"],[13.889,30.954,20.69,1.809,1.634,"the stock near $96 or near zero."],[13.889,33.439,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Q3 net loss was $183.2m ($1.55 a share) as R&D rose 85% to $166.8m."],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"VANQUISH-1 and -2 (about 5,500 patients, 78 weeks of weekly injection)"],[13.889,36.328,52.966,1.809,1.634,"complete in 2027. September’s maintenance study is the best new evidence:"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"17.8% weight loss after 21 weeks at 17.5 mg, and monthly dosing then kept 82–"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"90% of the loss against 61% on placebo. The tablet is weaker: its 13-week Phase"],[13.889,40.684,52.936,1.809,1.634,"2 lost 20% of treated patients to adverse events (13% on placebo), so we give it"],[13.889,42.128,52.934,1.809,1.634,"45%. Cash of $960m faces $259m of convertible notes and, Viking says, lasts"],[13.889,43.572,52.931,1.809,1.634,"through at least end-2027. We forecast an FY27E loss of $5.80 a share"],[13.889,45.016,36.009,1.809,1.634,"(consensus $5.21) and about $120m of cash at Dec-27."],[13.889,47.502,52.934,1.809,1.634,"The target averages a risk-weighted NPV to 2040 at a 9.4% cost of equity ($37)"],[13.889,48.946,52.959,1.809,1.634,"and the large-pharma forward P/E of 15.2x on probability-weighted 2035E"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"earnings ($105). The legs are far apart: the first gives the rest of the pipeline"],[13.889,51.834,52.966,1.809,1.634,"nothing, the second treats Viking as a going concern. Peak sales are the swing:"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"we assume $8.5bn (Zepbound runs at $21.4bn a year), and at half that the"],[13.889,54.722,52.962,1.809,1.634,"average is $20, below the price. Launch needs about $2.0bn more than Viking"],[13.889,56.167,52.964,1.809,1.634,"holds; raised at today’s price, the target falls to $54. We would be wrong if 78-"],[13.889,57.611,40.972,1.809,1.634,"week weight loss trails tirzepatide’s or discontinuations climb."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.758,68.709,0.999,1.022,0.915,"20"],[15.758,66.348,0.999,1.022,0.915,"30"],[15.758,63.998,0.999,1.022,0.915,"40"],[15.758,61.639,0.999,1.022,0.915,"50"],[17.8,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.424,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.293,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[31.901,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.944,70.575,3.827,1.275,1.111,"Viking ($)"],[25.551,70.575,7.626,1.275,1.111,"S&P 500 (rebased)"],[20.481,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.166,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.081,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[18.98,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−29.6%"],[23.664,72.8,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−7.3%"],[28.028,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−27.9%"],[32.945,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−27.7%"],[15.492,73.866,1.476,1.3